_:na304b073465740098022aec0efa0a0b7b14 <http://www.loc.gov/mads/rdf/v1#fieldOfActivity> <https://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85080300> .
_:na304b073465740098022aec0efa0a0b7b7 <http://www.loc.gov/mads/rdf/v1#citationNote> "(Irial Glynn, University Lecturer ; Dr. I.A. Glynn ; i.a.glynn@hum.leidenuniv.nl ; Irial Glynn (1979) completed his BA in archaeology and history in 2001 at University College Dublin (UCD). After working as a professional archaeologist in Ireland and France for a number of years, he returned to UCD to complete an MA in History on the decolonisation of India (2004). doctoral studies at the European University Institute in Florence ; He taught at University College Dublin until 2012. In 2013 he worked as a post-doctoral researcher on the Emigre project at University College Cork ; In January 2014, he started a two-year Marie Curie Fellowship at Leiden University's Institute for History. He has held visiting fellowships at the University of Oxford and New York University ; comparative history, economic history, migration history, social history)" .
