_:n22ba688293c34bdda310a42a4e0f4bc3b24 <http://www.loc.gov/mads/rdf/v1#occupation> <http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85025618> .
_:n22ba688293c34bdda310a42a4e0f4bc3b5 <http://www.loc.gov/mads/rdf/v1#citationNote> "Faculty Profiles (Rev. Dr. Jennifer Powell McNutt; she is Associate Professor of Theology and History of Christianity; a fellow in the Royal Historical Society; received her Ph.D. in History from the University of St. Andrews, an M.Div. from Princeton Theological Seminary, and a B.A. in Religious Studies from Westmont College; her research specializes in the history of the Church and Christian theology from the Reformation through the Enlightenment with particular expertise in John Calvin and his clerical legacy, the Reformed tradition, the relationship between Christianity and science, and the history of the Bible and the Reformation; she is also an ordained Teaching Elder in the Presbyterian Church (U.S.A.) and is co-president of McNuttshell Ministries, Inc.)" .
